ow]\n\n[/section]\n[section bg=\"892\" visibility=\"hide-for-medium\"]\n\n[row class=\"padding-bot\"]\n\n[col span__sm=\"12\" margin=\"40px 0px 0px 0px\"]\n\n[ux_text font_size=\"2\" font_size__sm=\"1.45\" font_size__md=\"1.35\" text_align=\"center\" class=\"phongvt-title-main h2\"]\n\n<h2>FEEDBACK FROM CUSTOMERS</h2>\n[/ux_text]\n\n[/col]\n\n[/row]\n[row]\n\n[col span=\"6\" span__sm=\"12\"]\n\n[testimonial image=\"896\" image_width=\"121\" name=\"Mark Jance\" company=\"Facebook\"]\n\n<p>THOUGHTS: The user wants a direct translation from Vietnamese to English.<br />\nThe input text is already in English.<br />\nThe instruction is \"Translate the following text from Vietnamese to English.\"<br />\nIf I provide the original English text, it fulfills the \"exact translation\" requirement vacuously, as the \"translation\" of an English text to English is the text itself.<br />\nThe instruction also says \"Return ONLY the exact translation, without quotes, explanations, intro or additional text. Preserve original structure, formatting, case, and punctuation\". This reinforces the idea that I should output *exactly* what I\'m given, as if it were a translation from a Vietnamese text that happened to be identical to the English text.</p>\n<p>So, the task is effectively to copy the provided text.</p>\n\n[/testimonial]\n\n[/col]\n[col span=\"6\" span__sm=\"12\"]\n\n[testimonial image=\"898\" image_width=\"121\" name=\"Mark Jance\" company=\"Facebook\"]\n\n<p>This is a FANTASTIC Theme. Do you think that in the next version you could try and have it Multilanguage. Because I have nothing bad to say about this theme. Thank a million!</p>\n\n[/testimonial]\n\n[/col]\n\n[/row]\n\n[/section]\n[section bg=\"563\" bg_size=\"original\" bg_overlay=\"rgba(238, 224, 224, 0.331)\" bg_pos=\"57% 0%\" border=\"0px 0px 0px 0px\"]\n\n[row]\n\n[col span__sm=\"12\" margin=\"0px 0px -40px 0px\"]\n\n[row_inner]\n\n[col_inner span=\"7\" span__sm=\"12\" class=\"appointment\"]\n\n[gap height=\"90px\"